q.en:
Little-endian systems store the low-order byte at the lowest address; big-endian systems store the high-order byte at the lowest address. What does this code print on a little-endian system and on a big-endian system, respectively?
unsigned x = 0xDEADBEEF;
unsigned char *p = (unsigned char *)&x;
printf("%X", *p);

q.zh:
計算機系統用小端（Little Endian）和大端（Big Endian）來描述多位元組資料的儲存地
址順序模式，其中小端表示將低位位元組資料儲存在低地址的模式、大端表示將高位位元組數
據儲存在低地址的模式。在小端模式的系統和大端模式的系統分別編譯和執行以下 C++代
碼段表示的程式，將分別輸出什麼結果？（ ）
unsigned x = 0xDEADBEEF;
unsigned char *p = (unsigned char *)&x;
printf("%X", *p);

q.en:
What does ack return for the input (2, 2)?
unsigned ack(unsigned m, unsigned n) {
  if (m == 0) return n + 1;
  if (n == 0) return ack(m - 1, 1);
  return ack(m - 1, ack(m, n - 1));
}

q.zh:
ack 函式在輸入引數“(2,2)”時的返回值為（ ）。
unsigned ack(unsigned m, unsigned n) {
if (m == 0) return n + 1;
if (n == 0) return ack(m - 1, 1);
return ack(m - 1, ack(m, n - 1));
}

